## What the change is

The continuation family mirrors the **JS prelude** shape (clojure has no generators, no `with`, no recursion-limit hook, so no `:depth`/`:base`/`:frame` accounting — `{:handlers}` only, 4-tuple frames, binary `try`). I confirmed every operator used (`conj`, `+`, `<=`, `nil?`, `get`, `assoc`, `=`) is a VM primitive (`yin/vm.cljc:404-423`) and `%capture` maps to `:vm/current-continuation` (`yang/core/uast.cljc:16,100`), so all new free names resolve through `module-spec`.

Three edits to `src/cljc/yang/clojure/prelude.cljc`:

**1. `runtime-keys`** — add `clj.rt/ctx`:
```clojure
'[clj.rt/state clj.rt/globals clj.rt/ctx])
```

**2. `clj/init!`** — allocate the ctx cell:
```clojure
(do (yin/def (quote clj.rt/globals) (cell/new {}))
    (yin/def (quote clj.rt/ctx) (cell/new (clj/ctx nil)))
    (yin/def (quote clj.rt/state) :clj/ready))
```

**3. New `;; ------------------------------------------------------------- escapes` section** (inserted between `clj/global-get` and the entry section), defining: `clj/ctx`, `clj/rt-ctx`, `clj/restore!`, `clj/handlers`, `clj/set-handlers!`, `clj/frame-depth`, `clj/frame`, `clj/pop-frame`, `clj/raise`, `clj/throw` (guest form — `throw` takes arbitrary values, so it is `clj/raise` under the guest name), `clj/unwind-to`, `clj/try`, `clj/try-finally`, `clj/call-ec`. The `:clj/no-handler` sentinel matches the js/py empty-stack terminal.

I also updated the ns docstring to add a fourth "surface" bullet documenting the family.

